  "interpretation": "The construction is an initial affine perturbation followed by unconstrained minimisation, not a maintained eigenstrain: the equilibrium metric of the potential is unchanged, so the inclusion relaxes back toward it and is held away only by lattice discreteness. Rescaling on the nominal amplitude therefore understates the field by 1/eta. The amplitude that a genuinely maintained eigenstrain would produce is given instead by the analytic Eshelby solution of stageG8, 2.14 MPa interior at 100 ppm."
